{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Anti-inflammatory", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Discovery: in silico mine the venom gland transcriptome library by comparing with known spider genomes for similar AMPs. Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is most similar (37.5%) to LtTx-1a k: 15%; c: 12%. GRAVY: -0.538; mol Wt: 7306.515; mol formula: C314H503N93O91S8; mol ex coeff: 1990. Chemical modification: four disulfide bonds are predicted: C1–C4, C2–C5, C3–C8, C6–C7. Activity: strongly active against E. coli (MIC 1 uM), P. aeruginosa (MIC 1 uM), B. cereus (MIC 1 uM), and S. aureus (MIC 8 uM). As strong as melittin. It also suppressed LPS-induced inflammation by down-regulating TNF-alpha, IL-1beta, and IL-6 MOA:bacteria: it permeated bacterial membranes and depolarized bacterial membranes of multiple bacteria. ROS release. In vitro Toxicity: bovine RBC: 10% hemolysis at 20 uM peptide. LDH release: up to 20 uM, it did not show toxicity to human adipose-derived mesenchymal stem cells (hADMSCs) and murine macrophage RAW264.7 cells.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "38136742", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Antibiotics (Basel). 2023 Dec 7;12(12):1708. doi: 10.3390/antibiotics12121708. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04196", "source_id": "AP04196", "source_numeric_id": "04196", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04196", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "The Identification of a Novel Spider Toxin Peptide, Lycotoxin-Pa2a, with Antibacterial and Anti-Inflammatory Activities.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
